"answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off on June 15th and a Phase 1 budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The project involves gathering innovative ideas by July 20th to leverage AI in data visualization. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase, to be discussed on August 5th. The team expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, welcomed on September 10th, and later added Mike Chen and Lisa Ray for machine learning and cloud computing expertise. Following the design phase, the development phase began next month, led by Omar Jensen. A major milestone was reached ahead of schedule with a successfully tested prototype for secure file sharing, with UI enhancements planned for October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. The project is now nearing its final stages."
